"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-08-20T09:39:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T09:23:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.8.dev3.official [51105ccbe]\n\n### System information\n\nFedora 44\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you have a popup with search bar enabled and a submenu that also have search bar enabled and you set focus to the search bar in the submenu and then move mouse back to the parent. Hover and press no longer works with the mouse.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/48b53ef6-e991-4bde-8634-54f12d8d202d\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Turn off display/window/subwindows/embed_subwindows\n2. Have a popupmenu with search bar enabled\n3. add a submenu that also have search bar enabled\n4. Set focus to submenu search bar\n5. move mouse back to parent popup\n6. Now you should have no hover and clicking on item will no trigger it\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[popup-search.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31258317/popup-search.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122637/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}